          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"skram-constance-ring-2b09d5b293401db7\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":4,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"Lorck explicitly avows that he loves Constance and stresses the seriousness and unexpectedly deep extent of that state, strongly supporting T. His immediate offer—“I give you myself, my life, my soul”—and request that she accept it give the declaration substantial courtship and relational-undertaking force, strongly supporting P. Although he is intensely emotional, the words are delivered as an insistent, developed avowal and offer; there is no positive evidence that their production is itself a reflex-like affective discharge, so E is unsupported.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The figurative offer of self, life, and soul could be read partly as passionate rhetoric rather than a determinate commitment, but the explicit invitation to accept it still provides strong P support.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Lorck directly addresses Constance with “Jeg elsker dig” during an unwanted declaration and proposal-like offer of himself.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Lorck’s declaration follows an earlier admission that his year-long infatuation has become a consuming passion. After Constance rejects his advances and asks him to stop, he repeats the avowal, calls it serious, offers her his entire self, and asks for acceptance. Thus the utterance combines an avowed emotional state with an attempted relational undertaking. Its force is coercively intensified by his threatening proximity, refusal to accept her resistance, and later accusations and physical restraint; those features characterize the interaction but do not require a category beyond T/P/E. Constance plainly experiences the scene as frightening and insulting rather than as welcome courtship.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg elsker dig, Constance — det er Alvor, ganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.”\",\"supports\":\"The explicit love avowal, assertion of seriousness, and claim that the feeling is deeper than Lorck himself knew strongly support T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, — vil du ikke ta imod det?”\",\"supports\":\"Lorck offers himself, his life, and his soul and asks Constance to accept them, supplying strong independent evidence of relational-undertaking force under P.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Before the highlighted utterance, Constance rejects him, asks him to stop, and tells him not to frighten her; Lorck then makes the declaration while standing pale and threatening before her.\",\"supports\":\"Establishes the coercive, unwanted courtship context while showing that this contextual misconduct does not alter the core utterance into an O case.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Lorck previously describes the feeling as a year-long infatuation that has become “en Lidenskab, som fortærer mig” (“a passion that consumes me”).\",\"supports\":\"Supports the presented depth of his loving state but, absent evidence of reflex-like verbal discharge, does not independently support E.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified as an explicit present-tense Norwegian love construction in Amalie Skram’s Constance Ring, with membership review KEEP at 0.99 confidence.\",\"supports\":\"Corroborates identification of the highlighted expression as the core explicit love utterance being classified.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the core force as both a serious avowal of love and an attempted relational offering. Emotional intensity and coercive delivery are adequately handled as context and do not establish E or create residual pressure for O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The analytical translation was used only to aid interpretation; quoted verbal evidence is grounded in the supplied source passage.\"}"
        }
